        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Industry context</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Operators need scale, speed and regional reach</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>MEA telecom operators are investing in backbone fibre expansion, 5G rollout and edge compute to serve growing data demand. These initiatives require deep engineering expertise, reliable supply chains and infrastructure partners who understand carrier-grade requirements.</p>
          <p>Interconnectivity between operators, submarine cable systems and international gateways is critical for regional data exchange. Operators need partners who can design, build and maintain the physical and logical infrastructure that connects networks across borders.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Use cases</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Where MEAICON makes the difference for telecom operators</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">5G edge site deployment at scale</h3>
          <p>MEA operators are rolling out 5G across urban and rural areas, requiring hundreds of edge compute sites with power, cooling, security and backhaul connectivity. MEAICON provides site readiness engineering, micro-data-centre deployment and integration services that accelerate edge rollout timelines. We handle site survey, power systems, rack infrastructure and monitoring — letting operators focus on radio and core network activation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Submarine cable and interconnect infrastructure</h3>
          <p>MEA is a critical junction for global submarine cable systems connecting Europe, Asia and Africa. Operators need landing station infrastructure, cross-connect systems and peering exchange capacity. MEAICON engineers landing station fit-outs, interconnect cabling, optical layer solutions and carrier hotel infrastructure — ensuring that international traffic flows reliably across borders and between operator networks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal grid-2 mt-8">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">NOC modernisation and operations support</h3>
          <p>As networks grow in complexity, operators need NOCs that can monitor fibre, wireless, edge and interconnect layers from a single pane of glass. MEAICON provides NOC engineering support, monitoring system integration and operational tooling — including automated alerting, ticket routing and capacity threshold management — backed by defined SLAs and escalation procedures.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">MEA telecom at a glance</h3>
          <p>MEA mobile data traffic is projected to grow at 30–40% annually through 2030, driven by 5G expansion, population growth and digital transformation. The GCC has fully launched 5G, with operators investing billions in edge and fibre infrastructure. Africa's mobile subscriber base exceeds 500 million, with submarine cable capacity growing to connect emerging markets. Saudi Arabia and the UAE are positioning as regional interconnect hubs, with data centre and peering capacity expanding rapidly to serve cross-border data exchange.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

