  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Real-world impact</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Sector scenarios & case studies</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>A Gulf-region telecom operator engaged MEAICON to deploy 5G edge compute nodes across a metropolitan area to support enterprise low-latency services. MEAICON engineered micro-data-centre sites at strategic aggregation points, each with carrier-grade power, cooling, and security infrastructure. The edge sites enabled the operator to offer sub-ten-millisecond latency for enterprise customers running real-time analytics, augmented reality applications, and autonomous vehicle telemetry processing. The deployment was phased to avoid disruption to live network operations, with each site activated and integrated into the NOC monitoring framework before traffic was migrated.</p>
          <p>For a North African national carrier, MEAICON designed an edge computing rollout spanning twelve regional sites along the country's fibre backbone. Each edge site hosted content caching, local break-out for enterprise VPNs, and IoT processing for smart city deployments in regional capitals. MEAICON engineered the interconnect architecture between edge sites and the core network, ensuring that capacity planning accommodated projected five-year growth in data demand without requiring incremental civil works.</p>
          <p>An East African regional operator engaged MEAICON to build interconnect infrastructure with a subsea cable landing station, expanding international bandwidth capacity and reducing transit costs. MEAICON engineered the carrier hotel infrastructure, cross-connects, and DWDM optical transport that linked the landing station to the operator's national backbone, enabling the operator to offer tiered latency and bandwidth products to enterprise and wholesale customers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Case study highlight</h3>
          <p>A regional telecom operator partnered with MEAICON to deploy edge computing infrastructure supporting 5G edge nodes and low-latency enterprise services across a major metropolitan market. The programme delivered carrier-grade edge sites with integrated NOC monitoring, enabling new revenue streams from enterprise low-latency services.</p>
